/-!
# Derived Chow's lemma

Let `A` be a ring and let `X` be a separated scheme of finite presentation over `A`. Around every
point `x` of `X` there is a derived Chow datum: an open `U ∋ x`, an open `V` of a projective space
`ℙᵐ_A`, a closed subscheme `Z ⊆ X ×_A ℙᵐ_A` of finite presentation whose first projection is an
isomorphism over `U` and whose second projection is a closed immersion over `V`, with the parts
of `Z` over `U` and over `V` equal, and a pseudo-coherent object `E` of `D(𝒪_{X ×_A ℙᵐ_A})`
supported on `Z` whose restriction to `X ×_A V` is that of `𝒪_Z` ([Stacks, Tag 0CSJ]).

The proof is the source's. The Noetherian case is
`AlgebraicGeometry.exists_chowDatum_isPseudoCoherent_of_isNoetherian`, where `E` is `𝒪_Z` itself.
In general, `X` descends to a separated scheme of finite presentation `X'` over a subring
`A' ⊆ A` generated by finitely many elements ([Stacks, Tags 01ZM and 01ZQ]), which is
Noetherian; the Noetherian datum for `X'` is pulled back to `X`, the complex being the derived
pullback of `𝒪_{Z'}`. That complex is pseudo-coherent by [Stacks, Tag 09U7], and supported on `Z`
because derived pullback is computed on derived stalks. Its restriction to `X ×_A V` is the
direct image of `𝒪` of the part of `Z` over `X ×_A V` by Tor-independent base change along a
closed immersion ([Stacks, Tag 0E23], which is the case of [Stacks, Tag 08IB] the source uses),
the Tor independence being [Stacks, Tag 0CTA].

## Main definitions

* `AlgebraicGeometry.HasDerivedChowDatum`: the conclusion of [Stacks, Tag 0CSJ] for a morphism
  `f : X ⟶ S` at a point of `X`.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.cohomologySupportedOn_derivedPullback`: derived pullback pulls back the
  support of the cohomology.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.derivedPushforwardSingleIsoOfIsAffineHom`: `Rf_*(M[0]) ≅ (f_*M)[0]` for `f`
  affine and `M` quasi-coherent.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.hasDerivedChowDatum_of_isPullback`: the limit step — a Noetherian-style
  derived Chow datum pulls back along a base change.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.exists_isPullback_isSeparated_finitePresentation_adjoin`: a separated scheme
  of finite presentation over `A` is the base change of one over a finitely generated subring.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.exists_derivedChowDatum`: **[Stacks, Tag 0CSJ]**.

## Implementation notes

Clause (5) is stated as an isomorphism between the restrictions, by derived pullback along the
open immersion `X ×_A V ⟶ X ×_A ℙᵐ_A`, of `E` and of `(b, c)_*𝒪_Z` placed in degree zero. The
derived categories are the standard model `HasDerivedCategory.standard`, seated at a raised
priority for the reason recorded in `DerivedChowLemma`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0CSJ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0CSJ)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0CTA](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0CTA)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0E23](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0E23)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 08IB](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/08IB)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 09U7](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/09U7)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01ZM](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01ZM)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01ZQ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01ZQ)
-/

